@inject ApiMetadata Api
@* Dialog's Overview, written by hand after Button's: the three ways to open it previewed in each
   mode, a form inside one (what a post does to an open dialog), the parts, then size, closing,
   a dialog inside a form, and DialogService (Interactive only). Accessibility and See also come from the
   doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A dialog is a window over the page that the user deals with before going back to the page, such as a short form or a question. For a panel that slides in from an edge, see <Anchor Href="docs/components/drawer">Drawer</Anchor>. For a small panel next to a button that doesn't block the page, see <Anchor Href="docs/components/popover">Popover</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Opening it</Heading>
<TextBlock>A dialog opens three ways: from a button, from a link, or from C#. For a button, add a <Code>DialogTrigger</Code> with the dialog's <Code>Id</Code>. For a link, add <Code>?dialog=</Code> and the id to the URL. From C#, set <Code>@@bind-Open</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="dialog-open" />
<List>
    <ListItem>The trigger and the link work on <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">static pages</Anchor>, with JavaScript off too.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>To change the key the link uses, set <Code>QueryKey</Code>. Closing the dialog removes the key from the URL. Set it to null to turn links off.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>To show a dialog when the page loads, such as a notice after a form post, set <Code>Open</Code> from the server.</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">A form in a dialog</Heading>
<TextBlock>A dialog often contains a short form, such as renaming a file, with its buttons in the dialog's footer. Put a <Anchor Href="docs/components/form">Form</Anchor> in the dialog, with its <Code>FormActions</Code> last. The buttons become the dialog's footer and still submit the form.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="dialog-rename" />
<List>
    <ListItem>A form post on static pages closes the dialog. With JavaScript off, the browser loads a new page. With IzzyBlazor's script, the script closes the dialog as the form posts.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>The script opens the dialog again when the response has errors in it.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>So the errors show with JavaScript off too, set <Code>Open</Code> yourself when the form post fails, as this example does in <Code>OnInvalidSubmit</Code>.</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">Header, body and footer</Heading>
<TextBlock>A dialog has a heading, a body, and a footer of buttons. For a plain heading, set <Code>Title</Code>. For a heading with an icon or a badge, add a <Code>DialogHeader</Code>. To lay out the body, put it in a <Code>DialogBody</Code> and set <Code>Gap</Code> and the other layout parameters. Put the buttons in a <Code>DialogFooter</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="dialog-parts" />
<TextBlock>The footer stays in view when the body scrolls. To run a table or list to the edges, set <Code>ContentPadding="0"</Code> on the dialog or <Code>Flush</Code> on its <Code>DialogBody</Code>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Size and placement</Heading>
<TextBlock>A dialog opens in the middle of the screen by default, or as a panel along an edge. To set its width, set <Code>Size</Code> (<Code>Sm</Code>, <Code>Md</Code>, <Code>Lg</Code>, <Code>Xl</Code> or <Code>Full</Code>), or <Code>Width</Code> for another width. To open it at an edge, set <Code>Placement</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="dialog-placement" />
<TextBlock>A <Anchor Href="docs/components/drawer">Drawer</Anchor> is a dialog that opens at an edge: the end edge by default, or another edge set by its <Code>Placement</Code>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Closing</Heading>
<TextBlock>The user closes a dialog with Escape, the close button, a <Code>DialogClose</Code>, or a click on the backdrop. For a form the user could lose with a stray click, set <Code>CloseOnBackdrop="false"</Code> to keep the dialog open when the backdrop is clicked. When the footer's buttons are enough, set <Code>ShowCloseButton="false"</Code>. Escape, the close button and a <Code>DialogClose</Code> still close it.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Inside a form</Heading>
<TextBlock>A dialog sometimes has to sit inside a form, such as a confirmation for that form's own submit button. Set <Code>InsideForm</Code> on it. Forms can't nest, so its close buttons then close it without submitting the form, and a submit button in it submits the form around it.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Inside</Code>
<TextBlock><Anchor Href="docs/components/confirm-button">ConfirmButton</Anchor> does this in one component.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Dialogs from code</Heading>
<TextBlock>On interactive pages, you can open a dialog from C# and wait for how it ends, such as asking a question before deleting. Inject <Code>DialogService</Code>. <Code>ConfirmAsync</Code> asks a question, and <Code>OpenAsync</Code> shows a component of yours. A <Code>DialogHost</Code> on the page or its layout shows them.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="dialog-service" />
<TextBlock>The page awaits the result:</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor" Title="EditPage.razor">@FromCode</Code>
<TextBlock>The component closes the dialog with its result, through the <Code>DialogInstance</Code> it receives:</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor" Title="EditName.razor">@Content</Code>
<TextBlock>Static pages can't open a dialog from code. Use a trigger, a link or <Code>Open</Code> there.</TextBlock>

@if (OverviewParts.Of(Component, Api).Count > 0)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Parts</Heading>
}
<OverviewParts Component="Component" />

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        <DialogTrigger For="invite">Invite people</DialogTrigger>

        <Dialog Id="invite" Title="Invite people">
            <Form Model="Invite" FormName="invite" OnValidSubmit="SendAsync">
                <TextField @bind-Value="Invite!.Email" autofocus />
                <FormActions>
                    <DialogClose>Cancel</DialogClose>
                    <Button Submit>Send invite</Button>
                </FormActions>
            </Form>
        </Dialog>
        """;


    private const string Inside = """
        <Form Model="Order" FormName="order" OnValidSubmit="PlaceAsync">
            ...
            <DialogTrigger For="confirm-order">Place order</DialogTrigger>
            <Dialog Id="confirm-order" Title="Place this order?" Size="DialogSize.Sm" InsideForm>
                Your card is charged $48.00.
                <DialogFooter>
                    <DialogClose>Cancel</DialogClose>
                    <Button Submit>Place order</Button>
                </DialogFooter>
            </Dialog>
        </Form>
        """;

    private const string FromCode = """
        @inject DialogService Dialogs

        @code {
            private async Task EditAsync()
            {
                var result = await Dialogs.OpenAsync<EditName>("Edit name", new() { ["Name"] = _name });
                if (!result.Canceled) _name = result.DataAs<string>();
            }
        }
        """;

    private const string Content = """
        <form @onsubmit="() => Dialog.Close(_name)">
            <input @bind="_name" aria-label="Name" autofocus />
            <DialogFooter>
                <Button OnClick="Dialog.Cancel" Variant="ButtonVariant.Outline" Accent="Accent.Neutral">Cancel</Button>
                <Button Submit>Save</Button>
            </DialogFooter>
        </form>

        @code {
            [CascadingParameter] public DialogInstance Dialog { get; set; } = null!;

            [Parameter] public string? Name { get; set; }

            private string? _name;

            protected override void OnInitialized() => _name = Name;
        }
        """;

}
